# Trivy Ignore File
# https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# AVD-DS-0026: HEALTHCHECK not required for development/utility containers
# DevContainer and tools images are interactive/short-lived, not production services
AVD-DS-0026

# DS-0002 / AVD-DS-0002: .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile
# Trivy emits this check with no file location, so a path filter never matches
# and an inline comment cannot attach to a missing USER line.
# The file is a ClusterFuzzLite build image. The OSS-Fuzz Go builder compiles
# the fuzz target and writes it to /out as root. A non-root USER breaks that
# build. The image is not deployed as a service.
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile sets USER vscode. images/tools/Dockerfile sets a
# non-root user of its own. This exception is for the builder image.
DS-0002
AVD-DS-0002
